---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/nics-is-not-sales";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "NICS is weather", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="NICS is weather. It is not the register. | FFL Intel"
  description="Background-check counts mix permits, used guns, and denials. Treating that volume like unit sales is how a forecast goes sideways."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.range}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3">
      Checks
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white text-balance mb-4">
      NICS is weather. It is not the register.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">
      A public FBI tally of background checks is useful climate. It is a terrible
      cash drawer.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="6 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.range)}
        alt="Betsy at the range"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full object-cover max-h-80"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>
        Every spring someone pastes a NICS chart into a dealer group and calls it
        demand. The chart is not lying. It is also not sales. Checks include
        permits in some states, used guns, transfers, multiple guns on one form,
        and denials. A hot March on that series can be paperwork. A cold March
        can hide a store that actually moved new units.
      </p>
      <p>
        Gearfire’s public case for the Firearm Sales Index is, on this point,
        fair: if you want to know what new guns rang, count new guns at the
        register. I will cite that print when Outdoor Wire or NSSF puts a number
        on a dated page. I will not pretend a check is a unit.
      </p>
      <p>
        And even a clean register series is still last month. The third number —
        what people typed and did not find — never shows up in either weather
        report. That is{" "}
        <a href={withBase("sell-through-vs-search-intent")} class={linkClass}
          >the ask</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Longer platform note, if you want the same argument next to Brand
        Intelligence:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gseNics} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >NICS vs firearm sales</a
        >{" "}
        on GunSearchEngine.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
